  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)-5,$  where \n$x$ is measured in degrees? Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)-5,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x=n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}}{3} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {60}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=n\\cdot {60}^{\u2218},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
